  "conclusions": [
    "neutral acts as a residual class on 3-way split votes: 465 zero-vote assignments corpus-wide (0.52%), 94.4% on 3-distinct-vote items, 99.1% labelled neutral; DS makes 14 zero-vote assignments on the contested 44 and 13 are wrong",
    "within the 14-item {obj x2, pos x2, neg x1} pattern on the contested set: DS sends 6 to neutral (zero neutral votes cast), all 6 wrong; MV's canonical-order tie-break (objective) is right on 9/9 human-objective items",
    "removing neutral (3-class DS) collapses the zero-vote symptom to empty-vote items only (30 corpus-wide, 0 on contested) yet contested accuracy improves just 22.7%->27.3% while MV stays at 45.5%: the catch-all is a symptom, not the cause",
    "28-cell prior sweep: contested accuracy flat in [0.227, 0.295], zero-vote rate flat 0.41-0.52% except under 10x class-prior shrinkage (0.12%) — structural, not tuning",
    "entropy routing: valid as pool discovery (DS errors concentrate in the routed pool; zero-vote items mean entropy 0.80) but weak within pool (AUC 0.659; tertile error rates 73/73/86%); MV entropy has no signal (AUC 0.465)",
    "no aggregator or routing change made; candidate fixes (MV/MACE primary on contested items, zero-vote veto, priors fit on adjudicated contested items) listed for the aggregator decision"
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "n=45 contested items; CIs are wide (±15-20 points)",
    "single human annotator; PROTOCOL §6 three-annotator adjudication not yet run",
    "contested set drawn from a high-entropy slice selected under the shipped DS posterior (DS-relative by construction)",
    "per-judge figures use derived votes with mixed-as-abstention; mistral 33.3% here vs 35.6% under vote-credited convention",
    "4 zero-vote 'objective' assignments shared by all aggregators trace to empty-vote items (no judge cast any vote), an index-0 default artifact"
  ]
